You hit this live: adding 'blog' to DIGITIKA_MODULES (in an earlier commit
of mine) without a matching entry in admin-nav.ts's MODULE_UI map meant
MODULE_UI['blog'] was undefined, and .href on undefined crashed the entire
admin sidebar (AdminSidebar -> admin/layout.tsx), taking down every /admin/*
page, not just blog. My bug from patch 0001.

- admin-nav.ts: added the missing 'blog' MODULE_UI entry
- Built the actual /admin/blog page + BlogAdminPage.tsx (list, create/edit
  modal, publish/unpublish toggle, delete) — this was flagged as a
  'follow-up, not built yet' two sessions ago; building it now since the nav
  literally points at it and you're the one hitting the gap live.
- Fixed a real bug in the API routes while wiring the UI to them:
  POST/PATCH /api/admin/blog were calling schema.parse() unguarded, so a
  validation error or duplicate slug (unique constraint) would 500 instead
  of returning a clean 400/409 the UI could show.
